Description: softisp: Split AWB from Combined Matrix
 Backport of upstream libcamera commit 569e3a41e9e46e3577942ea84951b98b26b79867.
 AWB gains and the CCM were folded into a single matrix, so a clipped white
 pixel was multiplied by CCM * diag(gains) whose rows no longer sum to 1;
 channels then saturate unevenly and the brightest highlights come out
 tinted. On the Surface Pro 8 front camera (OV5693, factory CCM, gains
 R=1.29 G=1.00 B=1.66) white clipped to RGB(255, 189, 255), i.e. pink.
 The gains are now a separate stage, clamped equally on all channels before
 the CCM. Rewritten by hand for 0.7.0: Vector::clamp() does not exist here,
 and 0.7.0's shaders subtract the black level without normalising.
Origin: upstream, https://git.libcamera.org/libcamera/libcamera.git/commit/?id=569e3a41e9e46e3577942ea84951b98b26b79867
Author: Kieran Bingham <kieran.bingham@ideasonboard.com>
